/**
@page systemd systemd integration

ascii-chat can run under systemd on Linux. The packaged units use journald for
stdout and stderr, disable terminal-only startup UI and update checks, and set
`/dev/null` as the explicit application log sink. This discard sink does not
open a file.

When systemd provides `NOTIFY_SOCKET`, the process sends `READY=1` and startup
`STATUS=` notifications. Support is optional at runtime, so the same binary
works outside systemd. Install the packaged units with
`scripts/install-systemd-confs.sh`; pass `--user` for user services and
`--uninstall` to remove them. System-wide changes require root.

The API profile uses the existing server mode; there is no separate API mode.
*/
